From a7b63ad185b2a16f275a88c1422af45f4daba592 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] avalanche: vote over SHA256-identified eCash mempool batches

Add Avalanche pre-consensus voting over frozen Merklix mempool overlay
batches (MSG_AVA_MEMPOOL_BATCH / avabatch).

Original-Commit: 30a53ada3e295ebb2e10f1bd7191108935972efd
Original-Patch: ecash/012
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Complete ordinary batch voting, inventory/visitor/build wiring and finalization dispatch with its native regressions; use user-required domain-separated SHA256 batch IDs and matching Python/native vectors. Preserve upstream eCash activation and legacy header semantics. Assign adaptive voting, quorum caching/policy, snapshot publication, treasury and unrelated sync fixtures to their explicit owners instead of hoisting future APIs.

Stack-Repair-Plan-v2: Parking remains enabled with exact non-coinbase set equality to ANY finalized batch for the same parent. Remove latest-batch count comparison. Honest blocks carry exactly one finalized batch; newer transactions wait for the next batch. A batch-only parked head needs a descendant: automatic retry requires candidate work strictly greater than max(ABC fork penalty,parked head work), with transient per-index state and no timer. Preserve Avalanche-finalized ancestry against work retry. Keep already-present descendants eligible for the same work/finality retry when their ancestor is newly batch-parked. Clear old-parent batch/finalized/conflict/epoch records, including conflict IDs whose primary records were evicted; unmined transactions remain eligible after an actual older-batch connection. Tests cover both sibling arrival orders, work retry, no-repark, finality and stale-parent cleanup.

